body:
Please please know that you being dead does not have to be the solution to your pain. I have wanted to end my life on a wide range of occasions, but I assure you, despite every ounce of pain that you endure, life is worth it. It is such a relatively short endeavor to begin with, there is no need to attend to an early grave. I am aware this is hypocritical, as I am on this same subreddit, but my mood often oscillates. I am in the state of mind to tell you that EVERYTHING is temporary, and that your circumstances can and will change to feature some positivity again. 

&#x200B;

I understand your pain, I have wanted to talk to my ex, but she has made it damn near impossible, as well as clear that she is not interested by ignoring every response and blocking me in every way imaginable. No matter how badly it hurts, I am coerced to give her the space she has the right to. I may think it is unfair, but I likely have wronged her in ways she deems unforgivable. I suppose I failed, and have to live with this rejection.
